title: "Coordination Control Loop Framework (CCL-F)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Landry"
    given-names: "Morgan"
    affiliation: "Waterside Net Solutions"
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-06-09
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
type: software
abstract: "A formal model of the organizational commitment layer: the process by which known safety signals are either converted into evidence-based, executable decisions or lost before irreversible execution. CCL-F distinguishes coordination failure from coordination non-instantiation, formalizes closure quality, and defines runtime-detectable indicators of revision rigidity and trajectory lock."
keywords:
  - organizational safety
  - coordination
  - sociotechnical systems
  - systems safety
  - STAMP
  - safety engineering
